.TH DU 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
du \- estimate file space usage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B du
.RB [ \-asbhc ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR n ]
.RI [ path ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B du
prints how much each directory under each
.I path
holds, everything inside it counted, deepest first and the
.I path
itself last.
Each line is a size, a tab, and the path.
With no
.IR path ,
it uses
.BR . .
.PP
Sizes are in 1 KiB blocks: each file takes its size rounded up to
whole blocks.
Symbolic links are counted as themselves and never followed (as GNU
.BR du 's
.BR \-P ).
A file given as a
.I path
is always printed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a
Print each file too, not only directories.
.TP
.B \-s
Print only a total for each
.I path
given (the same as
.BR "\-d 0" ).
.TP
.B \-h
Print sizes in human\-readable form, in powers of 1024 (for example
.BR 1.5K ,
.BR 2M ).
.TP
.B \-b
Print sizes in bytes, the files' real sizes, not rounded to blocks.
It takes precedence over
.BR \-h .
.TP
.B \-c
Print a grand total of all the
.IR path s
at the end, labeled
.BR total .
.TP
\fB\-d\fR \fIn\fR, \fB\-\-max\-depth\fR \fIn\fR
Print directories (and with
.BR \-a ,
files) only down to
.I n
levels below each
.IR path ;
everything deeper is still counted.
.PP
Single\-letter options may be combined, as in
.BR \-sh .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 if a path could not be read or an option was invalid.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
du \-sh /home
du \-ad 1 /lib
du \-sc /bin /lib
.fi
.SH NOTES
The
.B \-\-max\-depth=n
form is not supported; give the number as the next argument.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR df (1),
.BR ls (1),
.BR find (1),
.BR tree (1)
